From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Suno <engineering@projectSuno.org>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Continue: the offer, progress and result banner

One standard banner that changes in place (ADR-055; design-center
mockups/continue): "Continue from ThinkPad?" with the snapshot's apps
(24 px icons, up to six, then +N) and Continue / Not now of equal weight;
over windows already here, the line that it opens on a new desktop;
restoring, with the apps still to open dimmed, a progress bar over the
20 s placement budget and Stop; and the result, "Reopened 8 of 11
windows" with one line about what is outstanding, which Show grows into
the list in place: installing (with its progress), not available on this
device, didn't open in time (Open), opened without a document, windows
moved off a display that isn't here. A restore after restart on this
device shows nothing unless something failed, then one banner from
Desktop with Open <app> and Show. On the device continued from, "Your
windows continued on Surface", or the offer back when there is something
newer there.

The offer comes after unlock, resume and login from Connect Sync's
GetContinueOffer when another device's session is newer than this one's;
Continue takes it (TakeContinue, after a sync cycle) and restores it;
Not now declines it until a newer one. Snapshots record continuedFrom.

messageList.js: a notification can draw content below its body
(notification.SunoContent, built per message and rebuilt in place), with
its own buttons that change the notification in place instead of marking it
acted on and closing its card, equal-width or at the end of the row (a
closing row at the end sits 6 px under the content). The banner's time is
when its subject happened: the snapshot's for an offer, the continue's on
the device continued from.

Snapshots carry each app's name and icon, so a device without the app
still shows which app it is; for an app neither installed nor named, the
Depot's kept catalogue gives the name and Flathub's AppStream cache the
icon. The result after a restart on this device is an ordinary banner
(standard timeout, then the list, Do Not Disturb respected), shown as a
banner and after the first unlock.

Restore, from the real Suno Shell: a window on the same display at the
same place keeps its exact rectangle (the work area at login is not final
until the panel and dock reserve their space); an X11 window adopted
without a configure (mapped while Xwayland was starting) is placed when
shown; a window that arrives after the restore doesn't take the focus;
the focused window keeps the focus for 3 s against apps presenting late,
until the person types or clicks; apps that reopen their own windows get
3 s before being asked for more. The shield going up is the lock also for
an account without a password, whose shield shows without locking: its
session is saved then, and the offer comes when the shield goes down.
A session that ended during its restore at login (the shell or the
display manager restarted) is restored once more, never a third time.
A shutdown delay lock (logind Inhibit shutdown/delay) holds the shutdown
until its snapshot is written, so the session's apps are still there:
without it the shutdown snapshot could replace the session with an empty
desktop. Snapshots are written durably (synced before the rename), so one
taken as the lid closes or the power goes is on disk.
---
